# Copy this file to .env and fill in a token. .env is gitignored.
#
# Nike has no username/password API worth using — the web login is behind bot
# protection and a scripted sign-in gets blocked — so the sync script borrows a
# token from a browser session instead.
#
# Getting one:
#   1. Log in at https://www.nike.com and open a page that shows your activity,
#      e.g. https://www.nike.com/member/profile
#   2. Open DevTools -> Application -> Local Storage -> https://www.nike.com
#   3. Find the credential entry (a key with "credential" or "oauth" in the
#      name) and expand its JSON. Copy `refresh_token` if there is one,
#      otherwise `access_token`.
#      Failing that: DevTools -> Network, filter for `api.nike.com`, pick any
#      request and copy the value after "Bearer " in its Authorization header.
#      That one is an access token.
#
# A refresh token keeps working for months; the script trades it for a fresh
# access token on every run. An access token dies after about an hour, so
# you'd re-copy it each time. Prefer the refresh token if you can find one.

NIKE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Only needed if you couldn't get a refresh token.
# NIKE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
